    "Content": "The husbands\u0027 attempt to return to being \u0022Apex Predators\u0022 backfires spectacularly. By committing atrocities and failing…

…who wants to continue the rigid patriarchy and griffon superiority to the detriment of griffonesses and ponies, and that shows he is a fake revolutionary, just like his fake "Clothes for All" pledge (because Verany is a textile baron). Coltbert says nobles used to treat serfs as interchangeable objects of pleasure, just like Verany treats workers as replaceable cogs. Coltbert treats his suitors as unique and irreplaceable, every creature has asset specificity when it comes to romance and charm. This is proven economically too; farmers and artisans are not replaceable cogs, but have uniqueness that makes them productive.

Coltbert Reforms: the Predator's Dilemma was solved not by morality, but by the weaponization of Ambition and Asset Specificity."
